{
  "meta": {
    "title": "Reel — edit video, mark it up",
    "id": "reel-site",
    "aspect": "16:9",
    "fps": 30,
    "duration": 32.5,
    "design": "reel-site",
    "x_note": "Eighth film. A promo for the reel-editor site itself, cut from its own landing page (reference/). White theme by request: near-white paper (#FBFBFD) with the site's exact tokens — blue does the pointing, pink circles the hero claim, yellow sweeps the highlight, Kalam carries the handwritten asides. Every scene is AT MOST 3 SECONDS, so the film reads as quick cuts with entrances that finish inside the beat. First film to use the `html` element type: the AI code card and the stack chips are raw markup whose utility classes are compiled into the stylesheet at build time — no Tailwind runtime, no CDN. First film to author `ease` as the site's own cubic-bezier(.2,0,0,1) curve."
  },
  "design": {
    "style": "reel site",
    "x_note": "Tokens are the landing page's own :root values verbatim. One blue (#6965DB) does all the pointing; pink (#FF4D8D) appears only on the hero circle and the closing ring; yellow (#FFD84D) only as the marker band — a yellow that reads as text on paper would be a warning, so it never leaves the highlighter. No dark variant: the site is a white theme by request.",
    "tokens": {
      "bg": "#FBFBFD",
      "surface": "#FFFFFF",
      "surface-hi": "#F0EFFC",
      "ink": "#14161F",
      "mute": "#636879",
